// §14 entry 8 -- integer index on `textus` -> EXS-E0311.
//
// §5.1, verbatim (this fixture is that example, wrapped in a function):
//
//   firma t: textus = "café"
//   t.octeti().numerus()      // 5   bytes
//   t.scalares().numerus()    // 4   scalar values
//   t.grapha().numerus()      // 4   grapheme clusters
//   t[0]                      // EXS-E0311: textus has no integer index
//
// `octeti`, `scalares` and `grapha` are distinct types precisely so that a
// byte offset, a scalar-value offset and a grapheme-cluster offset can
// never be silently confused (§2.4: "Byte-index panic / grapheme
// miscount"). Indexing `textus` itself with a bare integer names none of
// the three, so it is rejected rather than guessing which one was meant.
//
// DEFERRED: needs the type checker (Stage 2) to know that `t` has type
// `textus` and that `textus` has no `[integer]` operator at all.
// compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both still empty; `exsc aedifica`, run
// directly against this file, exits 0 and reports nothing -- confirmed,
// not assumed.

publica functio primum_octetum(t: textus) -> octetus {
    redde t[0]
}

